# ===========================================================
# CODING STANDARDS
# ===========================================================

## TypeScript
- Strict mode ON. Zero `any` types — use `unknown` and narrow it
- All functions have explicit return types
- `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/primitives
- Entity types live in types/*.types.ts (e.g. types/task.types.ts)
- Database row types are generated into types/database.types.ts (`npm run db:types`)
- Use optional chaining ?. and nullish coalescing ?? everywhere

## Components
- Functional components only — no class components
- PascalCase file names: TaskCard.tsx
- kebab-case folder names: /features/task-board/
- Split a component when a part of it has its own job and can stand alone
- Never fetch data directly in JSX — delegate to a store or custom hook
- Never call Supabase from a component or event handler — go through the store action or hook
- Named exports for components, default exports for pages only

## Colocation Rule
- Used in one feature only → components/features/[feature]/
- Used in 2+ features → promote to components/common/
- Hook used in one component → can live next to it
- Hook used in 2+ places → promote to hooks/


# ===========================================================
# DATA LAYER — SUPABASE
# ===========================================================
# Backend = Supabase. Schema + RLS are in supabase/migrations/ (we own them).
# Full reference: CLAUDE.md (Data Access Map, State Management Map) + docs/backend-supabase.md.

## Base Setup
- Clients come from lib/supabase/ — never construct ad-hoc clients:
  - createClient() from lib/supabase/client.ts  → Client Components
  - createClient() from lib/supabase/server.ts  → RSC / Route Handlers / Server Actions
  - lib/supabase/admin.ts (service role) → server-only; bypasses RLS
- Config from env (see .env.example): NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
  - The anon key is public by design — RLS protects data. Never ship SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to the browser.
- Dates: ISO 8601 (timestamptz) / YYYY-MM-DD (date) — always parse with date-fns.

## Query & Error Handling
- Read/write via supabase.from("table") (PostgREST), scoped automatically by RLS.
- Stores write through optimistically: update the store, write to Supabase, and on
  error roll back and toast.error(..., { description: parseSupabaseError(error) }).
- RLS denial returns a Postgres error (no row / permission) → toast a friendly message; do NOT redirect.
- Auth: supabase.auth.signInWithPassword / signOut; session lives in httpOnly cookies via @supabase/ssr.
- 401 / expired session: handled by the root proxy.ts refresh (Next 16's renamed middleware); gate protected routes there.

## Authorization
- Enforced by RLS in supabase/migrations/0002_rls.sql and later migrations (the real wall).
- usePermissions() mirrors the matrix for UX only — keep the two in lockstep.

## Tables → stores
# See CLAUDE.md → Data Access Map (kept current there).


