# ===========================================================
# FORMS & VALIDATION
# ===========================================================

- Every form: React Hook Form + Zod schema
- Zod schemas: lib/validations/[feature].schema.ts
- RHF mode: onBlur (not onChange)
- Always show field-level error messages below each input
- Mark required fields with * in label
- Disable submit button while isPending — show spinner inside button
- Validate with Zod before writing; map Supabase/Postgres errors to RHF field errors where possible
- Multi-step forms: show "Step N of N" progress bar


# ===========================================================
# SECURITY STANDARDS
# ===========================================================
# Non-negotiable. Highest priority rules.
# UPDATE immediately when auth strategy or policies change.

## Authentication
- Supabase Auth via @supabase/ssr → session in httpOnly cookies ONLY
  NEVER localStorage, NEVER sessionStorage for tokens
- Sign in: supabase.auth.signInWithPassword (or OAuth / magic link)
- Token refresh: handled by root proxy.ts on each request (lib/supabase/middleware.ts)
- Logout: supabase.auth.signOut() → clears cookies → clear Zustand UI state
- Session expiry: modal warning at 5 min remaining

## RBAC
- Roles: admin | manager | member | viewer (profiles.role)
- usePermissions() hook: canCreate, canEdit, canDelete, canManageTeam, canExportProposals
- VIEWER role: HIDE action buttons entirely (not just disabled)
- Protected routes: gated in proxy.ts; data scoped by RLS
- UI RBAC is for UX only — RLS (supabase/migrations/0002_rls.sql) enforces real access

## Input Sanitization
- DOMPurify on ALL user-generated content rendered as HTML
- Never dangerouslySetInnerHTML without DOMPurify
- All inputs validated with Zod before writing to Supabase

## Request Security
- RLS on every table is the authorization wall — never disable it
- Service-role key is server-only — never expose it to the browser (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix)
- Rate-limit login: disable button 30s after 5 failures (Supabase also rate-limits auth)

## Security Headers (next.config.js)
- X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
- X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
- Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
- Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
- Content-Security-Policy: defined in next.config.js

## Sensitive Data Rules
- Never log PII to console
- Never pre-fill password fields from stored values
- Exports: stream from server, never assemble client-side fully
- Never expose user ID or role in URL params

## Dependencies
- npm audit before every deployment — fix HIGH/CRITICAL immediately
- Pin major versions in package.json


# ===========================================================
# UI/UX STANDARDS
# ===========================================================

## Visual Hierarchy
- One primary CTA per page (shadcn variant="default")
- Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48px (p-1 through p-12)
- Always left-align body text and table data — never center
- Group content with whitespace, not just borders

## Typography Scale
- Page title:      text-2xl font-semibold
- Section header:  text-lg font-medium
- Body / labels:   text-sm
- Meta / captions: text-xs text-muted-foreground
- Max 2 font weights per page

## Color Tokens
Use shadcn semantic tokens only — never raw hex in classNames
- Text:     text-foreground / text-muted-foreground
- Surfaces: bg-background / bg-card / bg-muted
- Borders:  border
- Danger:   text-destructive / bg-destructive
- Brand:    text-primary / bg-primary

## Task/Project Status Colors
- Defined once in lib/constants/task-status.ts (TASK_STATUS_META: Tailwind class + hex
  side by side). Read them from there; never write a status colour inline.

## Loading States
- Every data-fetching component MUST have a Skeleton matching its shape
- Never full-page spinners — skeleton the content region only
- Mutations: disable button + spinner inside
- 200ms minimum delay before skeleton (prevents flicker on fast connections)

## Empty States
- Every list, table, and board MUST have a designed empty state
- Structure: Lucide icon (size=48) + heading + subtext + CTA button
- Use text-muted-foreground for copy

## Feedback & Micro-interactions
- All actions: immediate visual feedback < 100ms
- Success: toast.success() — auto-dismiss 3s
- Error: toast.error() — persist, show retry if relevant
- Destructive actions: ALWAYS confirmation dialog first
- Use optimistic updates for status changes and drag-drop reordering

## Tables
- Required: column sorting, row hover, skeleton, empty state
- Show: "Showing 1–20 of 143 results"
- Truncate long cells with truncate + Tooltip for full text
- Sticky header on scroll
- Bulk actions: floating action bar above table

## Modals
- Always use shadcn Dialog — never a custom modal
- Always X close button top-right
- Form modals: do NOT close on backdrop click (data loss risk)
- shadcn built-in transitions only

## Confirmations
- Destructive dialog must name exactly what will be deleted
- Provide Undo via Sonner toast (5s window) before permanent action


# ===========================================================
# MOBILE RESPONSIVENESS
# ===========================================================

## Breakpoints
- base (0–639px):  Mobile — single column, stacked, full-width
- sm   (640px+):   Large mobile tweaks
- md   (768px+):   Tablet (iPad portrait) — still narrow once the rail is shown
- lg   (1024px+):  Desktop — full sidebar + content layout
- xl   (1280px+):  Wide desktop

## Navigation
- < md:  no sidebar — bottom tab bar + slide-over drawer
- md–lg: 64px icon rail (w-16; labels hidden, title tooltips keep icons identifiable)
- lg+:   full sidebar with labels (lg:w-56, xl:w-64)

## Layout Rules
- Never fixed pixel widths — use w-full max-w-[X] mx-auto
- Tables: wrap in overflow-x-auto w-full div
- Cards: grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 / lg:grid-cols-3 — gate multi-column grids on lg:,
  because the content area on a tablet is far narrower than its viewport
- Forms: single column always on mobile
- Check every page at 375px before calling it done (CLAUDE.md rule 5)

## Touch Targets
- All interactive elements: minimum 44x44px (min-h-11 min-w-11)
- List item links: py-3 px-4 minimum padding
- Drag-and-drop: enable @dnd-kit pointer sensor for touch

## Input Types for Mobile Keyboards
- Email: type="email"
- Phone: type="tel"
- Numbers: type="number"
- URL: type="url"

## Heavy Views on Mobile
- Gantt: keeps its chart on mobile, inside its own horizontal scroller with swipe hints
- Calendar: keeps its month grid (it fits 375px)
- Task tables: card-stack as mobile alternative

## Performance on Mobile
- Lazy-load heavy components via dynamic():
  Gantt, export modals, rich text editors
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion
- loading="lazy" on all below-fold images
- Test on throttled 3G before marking complete


# ===========================================================
# ACCESSIBILITY (WCAG 2.1 AA)
# ===========================================================

- All interactive elements: keyboard-navigable + visible focus ring
- All images: descriptive alt text
- Semantic HTML: nav, main, aside, section, article, button
- Never div/span as clickable without role and tabIndex
- Color contrast: AA minimum — verify all custom colors
- Never convey info through color alone — pair with icon or label
- ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
- Focus trap in open modals (shadcn handles this — do not override)


# ===========================================================
# PERFORMANCE
# ===========================================================

- Lazy-load heavy components with dynamic():
  const GanttView = dynamic(() => import('../gantt/GanttView'), { ssr: false })
- React.memo for expensive list item components
- useMemo / useCallback only for proven bottlenecks — not by default
- Next.js Image component for all images
- Paginate ALL lists — never fetch unlimited records
- Prefetch on hover for predictable navigation routes


# ===========================================================
# TESTING
# ===========================================================

- Playwright (`npm run test:e2e`, specs in e2e/ — see e2e/README.md). It runs against
  LIVE Supabase + Zoho: everything a test creates is prefixed "[E2E]" and deleted in
  teardown, it never touches pre-existing data, and the Zoho push is never automated.
- Pure logic (lib/) is tested directly in Playwright specs, without a browser.
- Required per feature:
  - Happy path (data loads, renders correctly)
  - Loading state renders skeleton
  - Empty state renders when no data
  - Error state shows error message
  - Form validation blocks submission with invalid data
- Never test implementation details — test behavior only


# ===========================================================
# NAMING CONVENTIONS
# ===========================================================
# UPDATE when new file types or patterns are introduced

| Thing              | Convention               | Example                  |
|--------------------|--------------------------|--------------------------|
| Components         | PascalCase               | TaskCard.tsx             |
| Page files         | lowercase                | page.tsx, layout.tsx     |
| Hooks              | camelCase + use prefix   | useProjects.ts           |
| Supabase helpers   | lib/supabase/*.ts        | client.ts, server.ts     |
| Zustand stores     | kebab-case + -store.ts   | tasks-store.ts           |
| Zod schemas        | camelCase + .schema.ts   | profile.schema.ts        |
| Route paths        | kebab-case               | /projects/[projectId]    |
| Utility functions  | camelCase                | formatDate.ts            |
| Types/Interfaces   | PascalCase               | interface TaskResponse   |
| Env variables      | SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE     | NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL  |


# ===========================================================
# ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ===========================================================
# Never commit .env.local
# UPDATE when new env vars are added

Example `.env.local` (see .env.example; never commit real values):
- NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
- NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key      # public; RLS protects data
- SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key         # server-only; never NEXT_PUBLIC_
- NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=Timeline Estimator
- NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development
- Zoho and PBS server-only variables: see CLAUDE.md → Zoho / PBS sections


# ===========================================================
# WHAT NOT TO DO
# ===========================================================

- Never fetch data directly in a component — always use a store or hook
- Never store tokens in localStorage or sessionStorage
- Never use useEffect to sync server state — that is React Query
- Never use the any type
- Never hardcode strings that belong in constants or env vars
- Never install moment.js — use date-fns
- Never put business logic in components — hooks or utils
- Never skip loading, error, and empty states
- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without DOMPurify
- Never delete on first click — always confirmation dialog
- Never push directly to main — feature branches and PRs only
- Never use raw hex colors — use semantic Tailwind tokens
- Never build a custom modal — use shadcn Dialog
- Never render user HTML without sanitization
- Never fetch unlimited records — always paginate


